WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.560
When you walk into the exam

00:02.560 --> 00:04.760
and you're under a bit of pressure,

00:04.760 --> 00:06.020
you're a bit stressed,

00:06.020 --> 00:08.200
30 seconds of reading can save you

00:08.200 --> 00:10.120
from describing the wrong thing.

00:10.440 --> 00:12.920
Here's how I would spend them.

00:13.500 --> 00:15.620
First, look at the title.

00:15.820 --> 00:19.420
It tells you what's measured, where and when,

00:19.420 --> 00:21.580
and then you will paraphrase that

00:21.580 --> 00:23.220
in the introduction.

00:24.220 --> 00:27.160
Next, look at the horizontal axis.

00:27.160 --> 00:29.060
This is the time,

00:29.060 --> 00:32.220
so 2004 to 2024.

00:32.860 --> 00:35.280
Then look at the vertical axis.

00:35.280 --> 00:36.240
This is the quantity,

00:36.240 --> 00:38.080
and here is its unit:

00:38.080 --> 00:39.920
the percentage of adults.

00:40.520 --> 00:42.220
Now for the legend.

00:42.220 --> 00:44.160
It tells me which line is which.

00:44.160 --> 00:46.620
The solid green line is online,

00:46.620 --> 00:49.020
and the dashed line is print.

00:49.900 --> 00:51.920
Finally, the data point.

00:51.920 --> 00:54.420
Let's have a look at one with its unit.

00:55.280 --> 00:58.800
In 2012, 45% of adults

00:58.800 --> 01:00.520
read the news online.

01:01.800 --> 01:03.540
When I was an examiner,

01:03.540 --> 01:05.240
I saw good answers lose marks

01:05.240 --> 01:06.900
because a candidate wrote

01:06.900 --> 01:10.100
‘it rose from 18 to 74’.

01:10.100 --> 01:11.360
18 what?

01:11.360 --> 01:14.620
Always add the unit: 18% to 74%.

01:14.880 --> 01:17.260
And you can use the symbol

01:17.260 --> 01:18.320
or you can write the word.

01:18.320 --> 01:19.060
Both are fine,

01:19.060 --> 01:20.920
and you can interchange those as well

01:20.920 --> 01:21.820
if you like.

01:21.820 --> 01:24.840
So: the title, the axes,

01:24.840 --> 01:26.880
the units and the legend.

01:26.880 --> 01:29.940
On the right page, find each part of the graph,

01:29.940 --> 01:31.570
then choose the right unit.
